  "interpretation_limits": "Aquarium-trade fish; most specimens juveniles or subadults. Housing 26 ± 1 °C, 12 h light/dark; test freshwater approximately 26 °C. Fish 10 cm below surface in a vertical steel tube (1.15 m high, 22 cm diameter, water height 1.12 m), underwater speaker at bottom, soundproof chamber. Fifteen test frequencies 50, 150, 300, 600, 900, 1200, 1500, 1800, 2100, 2400, 2700, 3000, 3300, 3600 and 4000 Hz; levels up to 164 dB re 1 µPa, attenuated in 6 dB steps. Hydrophone calibrated sound pressure at the previous fish-head position; particle motion was not quantified. Dead-fish controls produced no AEP responses. Table 1 N counts responding individuals at each frequency, not a constant sample size. SD is standard deviation, not SEM. Response endpoints are the lowest/highest tabulated frequencies with responses, not universal lower/upper hearing limits or a continuous behavioural passband. No thresholds are tabulated at 4000 Hz; missing cells are not zero thresholds. Do not convert underwater dB re 1 µPa to airborne microphone levels or perceived loudness.",
